# The evaluation corpus and the model files are inputs, not evidence: wikitext-2 is a
# public download and the GGUFs are built from it by the scripts here. Committing 18 MB of
# retrievable text to carry a 100 KB result would make the repository worse at the one job
# it has, which is letting someone read what was measured.
#
# Everything that IS evidence - the runners, RESULTS.md and every raw output under
# results/ - stays tracked.
wikitext-2-raw/
wikitext-2-raw-v1.zip

# Quantized model files, produced by ppl-sweep.sh from a downloaded F16. Hundreds of MB.
models/
out/
*.gguf

# Kept: llama-1b.imatrix and calibration_datav3.txt. Both are small, and the imatrix is the
# calibration artefact that makes the imatrix-vs-stock comparison in RESULTS.md
# reproducible rather than merely described.
